  UniXNU-turnip's work tree .cache/mesa-work with UniXNU-turnip's patches/mesa (21, Droid-VM/UniXNU 527b8b7a3119) and macOS-DroidVM's
  patches/mesa-macos (0001 log allocation failures, 0002 virtgpu accelerator class) applied. Our changes on top:
  tooling/metal/turnip-a830/mesa/0001-turnip-darwin-native-a830.patch, 0002-turnip-darwin-tu-debug-file.patch,
  0003-turnip-darwin-failures-on-stderr.patch (2026-11-11: a lost device's reason and the kernel calls that fail on stderr in a
  release build, rate-limited), 0004-turnip-darwin-max-bo-size-limits.patch (the kernel's 256 MiB per-object limit as
  maxMemoryAllocationSize, maxBufferSize and maxResourceSize, larger BOs refused before the kernel), 0005-turnip-darwin-tu-debug-boot-arg.patch
  (piano-tu-debug=<flags>|none on the boot line before the seed's tu-debug file), 0006-turnip-darwin-device-window.patch (2026-11-12:
  the device's GPU window is its own connection's, not the enumeration probe's, whose slot may differ),
  0007-turnip-darwin-sysmem-feedback-flush.patch (2026-11-12: in a sysmem pass a draw whose fragment shader reads an input attachment
  of the subpass first cleans the CCU, invalidates UCHE and waits for the earlier draws' writes; TU_DEBUG=nofbflush / fbflushall),
  0008-turnip-darwin-object-limit-window.patch (2026-11-12: the per-object limit is Query's max_bo_bytes within the connection's GPU
  window, the device's own connection's when it differs from the probe's; a BO past its cache budget asked at its own size, not its
  size class; the largest BOs on stderr; tu_darwin_limits for the Metal frontend),
  0009-turnip-darwin-idle-trim-reclaim.patch (2026-11-12: cached BOs older than TU_DARWIN_BO_CACHE_AGE_MS and freed BOs whose fence
  passed go back by a one-shot timer armed only while something is held; cache budgets by the connection's window; a BoAlloc that
  finds no memory asks every GPU process for its cache through the Darwin notification org.unixnu.piano.gpu-reclaim and is tried
  again over about 120 ms)
  0010-turnip-gen8-tex-line-offset-bits.patch: Mesa 7ea5e51c8a301a15202e28fef114e4c4055bc329 (MR44151), byte pitches in bits;
  0011-turnip-gen8-multiplane-ubwc-base.patch: Mesa d286f87b1641abce126337f99caa13b11ae8ef5b (MR43965), combined UBWC Y base
  for gen8 multi-plane descriptors, with actual-plane-count collection and unused V clearing informed by Mesa
  cbdef9823c88c9daf5f90d0c2ccd0b5ff2c57d7c (MR44145). Upstream: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa.
  (MIT, as the files).
  0012-turnip-darwin-capacity-recovery.patch (ours, MIT, Leo Zhang): one bounded reclaim/retry policy for VA, BO allocation,
  host import, GPU mapping and heap admission; preserves native cleanup/retirement gates and lost-device status. A cooldown
  still permits progress after local capacity was returned. Removes a duplicate BO finish on lazy heap refusal. Exports a
  versioned per-process capacity census for opt-in frontend qualification logging. No VA-window/backing change.
  0013-turnip-darwin-bo-clear-under-lock.patch (ours, MIT, Leo Zhang, 2026-11-21): darwin_bo_finish clears the BO's struct under the
  retire lock before its record can reach the ring and the cache (upstream msm's tu_bo_make_zombie order; the late clear wiped a BO
  another thread had just taken from the cache: WindowServer's handle-0 Submit); piano-tu-bo-clear=early|late (boot line, else
  /private/var/ngpu/debug/tu-bo-clear) keeps the old order for an A/B; a submit entry with a cleared BO is refused in user space
  by name; finish/init race lines, inert until they fire.
  0014-turnip-darwin-cs-reserve.patch: keeps a bounded reserve of mapped command-stream BOs for the render server.
  0015-turnip-darwin-private-tier.patch: requests private backing only for GPU-only blit scratch when the kernel advertises
  support. The optional request uses BoAlloc's existing contiguous field and keeps the ABI v2 layout.
  0016-turnip-render-mode-for-attachment-memory.patch: the board's patches/mesa patch of that name (Droid-VM/UniXNU wip/droidvm, one of the two that
  are left over against the pinned 21), with one context line adapted to this Mesa's three-argument tu_trace_end_render_pass. It is the Mesa half of
  NativeMetal's 0020, which this bridge series needs; read docs/results-2026-11-27-metal-bridge-inputs-pinned-to-one-line.md (MIT, as the file).
  Build options: UniXNU-turnip build-turnip-macos-piano.py's, with -Dtu-darwin-abi-dir pointing at the ABI below.
