Frontend (MIT): UniXNU-turnip drivers/AdrenoMetal (NativeMetal fb063de per the VM's recipe; upstream https://github.com/UniXNU/AdrenoMetal).
  Our change on top, after macOS-DroidVM's scripts/piano-frontend-patch.py: tooling/metal/turnip-a830/frontend/
  0001-frontend-console-rate-limit-serial-concurrent-compute.patch (2026-11-11, MIT as the file: NBLOG's stderr copy rate-limited per
  call site, "no device answer" to the unified log only, a concurrent compute encoder run serially instead of refused). With it the
  plugin executable is linked here (objects without objc_msgSend selector stubs, so the link is reproducible), not taken from the VM.
  0002-frontend-render-barrier-policy.patch (2026-11-12, MIT as the file: piano-metal-barriers=all|small|none or
  /private/var/ngpu/debug/render-barriers for the render-pass barriers of panel-sized surface passes, each one left out on stderr).
  0003-frontend-surface-texture-sizes-limits.patch (2026-11-12, MIT as the file: no fixed cap on two-plane YCbCr surface textures,
  every refused or large texture, buffer and surface texture on the console with its geometry and the runtime's memory for it, the
  device's texture dimensions and memory figures answered from Turnip's tu_darwin_limits, a limits line per process).
  0004-frontend-function-formatted-description.patch (MIT, ours: NBFunction descriptions for Metal pipeline formatters;
  context from UniXNU-turnip 527b8b7a31192df14b96d10a70c339845ed2cd12).
  0005-frontend-quartzcore-generic-texcoords.patch (MIT, ours: keep the generic QuartzCore vertex matrix bindings when Metal omits
  the two optional texcoord count constants; context from the same UniXNU-turnip revision).
  0006-frontend-bounded-import-reclaim.patch (ours, MIT, Leo Zhang): byte/LRU/idle bounds on optional IOSurface import retains,
  complete runtime backing counts, GPU pressure notification to frontend/runtime, and one capacity-only retry after allocation
  locks unwind. The opt-in client-mem marker enables periodic frontend/backend census records. Real live ownership, fences,
  leases and the terminal WindowServer capture failure boundary are unchanged; this is not a terminal-OOM capture fallback.
  0007-pressure-surface-residency.patch and SurfaceResidency.h (ours, MIT): piano-surface-residency=1 lets pressure drop idle shader-read IOSurface
  texture generations; the original IOSurface supplies content on the next bind. Commands lease a generation until completion;
  writes, views, CPU access and indirect handles pin it. The runtime, Turnip retire queue and kernel still own actual BO cleanup.
  0008-frontend-windowserver-encode-thread.patch (ours, MIT: the WindowServer encode-thread handshake, gfx/ws-encode3).
  0009-frontend-compiler-additional-arguments.patch (2026-11-22, MIT, ours: the additional compiler arguments a Metal client sets, Core
  Image's runtime-header definitions among them; the reverted 0006 of 2026-11-18, 3be98315/afe114a5, renumbered) and
  0010-frontend-function-reflection.patch (2026-11-22, MIT, ours: NBFunction returnType/arguments for visible functions from the
  function's own AIR, read by tooling/metal/turnip-a830/frontend/AirSignature.h, ours, MIT; nil and one log line when the AIR states
  none or a type outside the set qualified against Apple's Metal). Context: the same UniXNU-turnip revision.
  0011-frontend-browser-gpu-mac2.patch (ours, MIT): Mac2 for caller images with an allowlisted ANGLE or Dawn library basename
  or Chromium framework directory.
